Notebook[{
Cell["Stabilizer Codes, Cross-Checked Against Stim", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
The shipped QuantumFramework stabilizer engine agrees with Stim where they \
overlap, and the Wolfram Language carries a symbolic parameter that a numeric \
stabilizer simulator structurally cannot.\
\>", "Subtitle",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: Aug 25, 2026)", "Author",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Wolfram Research Inc, USA", "Affiliation",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: How This Notebook Flows", "Subsection",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This notebook is a computation-first tour of the stabilizer layer that \
ships in the QuantumFramework paclet, checked against ",
 ButtonBox["Stim",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://github.com/quantumlib/Stim"], None}],
 ", the field-standard stabilizer simulator. It runs in two movements. Part A \
takes the shipped ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 " engine on the standard small codes (the three-qubit bit-flip and \
phase-flip codes, the nine-qubit Shor code, the five-qubit perfect code, and \
the seven-qubit Steane code) and shows, against Stim, that its stabilizer \
generators form a consistent group and its syndromes agree across every one- \
and two-qubit error, while an exact test on the state vector confirms every \
codeword carries the correct sign. Part B then builds an exact code analysis \
from GF(2) first principles in a handful of small functions, uses it to \
compute the exact code distance and a minimum-weight witness, checks the \
witness against Stim, and closes with the one move a numeric simulator has no \
answer for: carrying a symbolic parameter, so a statement about a whole \
infinite family of codes, or a continuous error angle, is settled \
symbolically rather than one instance at a time."
}], "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The division of labor is the honest one. Stim owns scale and speed: \
sampling large circuits, benchmarking decoders, estimating thresholds over \
thousands of qubits. This layer owns the exact and the symbolic corner: the \
exact minimum distance (which is NP-hard, so it lives at small ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 " by mathematical necessity), a sign-exact stabilizer state, and a symbolic \
parameter carried through the whole analysis. The two agree wherever they \
overlap, and that agreement is what makes the exact answers trustworthy and \
the symbolic ones worth reaching for. Neither tool competes with the other; \
each does what the other cannot."
}], "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before we start, a few notes on the environment. This is a live Wolfram \
notebook: evaluate the cells from top to bottom. Some cells define objects \
(the code table, a handful of small symplectic functions, a Python session \
running Stim) that later cells use, so order matters. My suggestion is to \
read each output and its meaning first, and only then unpack the input code \
that produced it. You are not locked into the codes as given: feed in your \
own stabilizer generators, push the symbolic family further, and re-run. If \
you have questions, reach out at ",
 ButtonBox["quantum@wolfram.com",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["mailto:quantum@wolfram.com"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell["Prerequisites and How to Read This", "Subsection",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "You should be comfortable with the stabilizer formalism at the level of a \
first course: Pauli operators, stabilizer generators, the codespace as their \
joint ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 " eigenspace, and logical operators as the normalizer modulo the stabilizer \
group. The binary symplectic picture (each Pauli as a vector over GF(2), \
commutation as a symplectic inner product) is built up from scratch in Part \
B, so no prior fluency there is required. The Stim cross-check calls Python \
through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ExternalEvaluate",
   BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
   ButtonData->{
     URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/ExternalEvaluate.html"], 
     None}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 "; if you do not have Stim installed, those cells say so and you can skip \
them, keeping the shipped-engine outputs and the from-scratch re-derivation \
as your checks."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell["Part I: A Shipped Engine and an Open Niche Beside It", "Section",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A stabilizer code on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 " physical qubits is defined by a set of commuting Pauli operators, its \
stabilizer generators. The codespace is their simultaneous ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " eigenspace, and if there are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 " independent generators the code stores ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 " logical qubits. An error is ",
 StyleBox["detectable", "TI"],
 " when it anticommutes with at least one generator (it flips that \
generator's measured eigenvalue, a syndrome bit), and ",
 StyleBox["undetectable", "TI"],
 " when it commutes with all of them. The dangerous errors are the \
undetectable ones that still act nontrivially on the codespace: these are the \
logical operators, and the code distance is the weight of the lightest one."
}], "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "QuantumFramework ships a compiled stabilizer engine, ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 ", built on the Aaronson-Gottesman tableau. It carries a stabilizer state as \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 " bits rather than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 " amplitudes, applies Clifford gates and measurements in polynomial time, \
and already comes with the standard codes as named states. That engine is \
fast and scales; this notebook is not about its speed. It is about two things \
speed does not settle: does it get the ",
 StyleBox["signs", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["syndromes", "TI"],
 " exactly right, checked against an independent engine, and can the \
surrounding language say something a stabilizer sampler cannot say at all."
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Why is exactness worth isolating when Stim samples so well? Because \
computing the exact minimum distance of a stabilizer code is NP-hard \
(Kapshikar and Kundu, ",
 ButtonBox["arXiv:2203.04262",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.04262"], None}],
 "), so any tool that returns the ",
 StyleBox["exact", "TI"],
 " answer is confined to small codes no matter how it is written. That is not \
a limitation to apologize for; it is the shape of the problem, and the \
textbook codes are exactly where an exact treatment earns its keep. And why \
symbolic generality? Because a numeric simulator represents one concrete code \
at a time: fixed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 ", fixed generators, fixed angles. A symbolic engine can carry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " as a symbol and settle a statement about an entire infinite family \
symbolically rather than one instance at a time, or carry an error angle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 " and return a syndrome expectation as an exact function of it. Neither is a \
thing Stim is built to do, and neither competes with what Stim is built to do."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell["\<\
Load the framework from a local checkout (adjust the path to your own), and \
build the Steane code as a shipped stabilizer state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
  "PacletDirectoryLoad", 
   "[", "\"\</Users/mohammadb/Documents/GitHub/QuantumFramework\>\"", "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"steane", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", "\"\<SteaneCode\>\"", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"steane", "[", "\"\<Stabilizers\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->506665461,ExpressionUUID->"04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"IIIXXXX\"\>", ",", "\<\"XIXIXIX\"\>", ",", "\<\"IXXIIXX\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"IIIZZZZ\"\>", ",", "\<\"ZIZIZIZ\"\>", ",", "\<\"IZZIIZZ\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"ZZZZZZZ\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[2]= ",
 CellID->855724595,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The object is the codeword ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    SubscriptBox["0", 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],
 ", carried as its stabilizer group. The first three generators are pure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 "-checks and the next three pure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 "-checks, the defining CSS structure of the Steane code; the seventh, the \
all-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 " string, is the logical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 " that pins this particular codeword inside the two-dimensional code space. \
Reading the parity checks apart from the logical is the one bookkeeping step \
the rest of Part A rests on."
}], "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell["\<\
Part II (Part A): The Shipped Stabilizer Layer, Cross-Checked Against Stim\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Collect the five codes into one table. The five-qubit, Steane, and Shor \
codes ship as named ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 " states; the two three-qubit repetition codes are not named states, so we \
build them directly from their generators. For each we record the shipped \
state, its parity checks (the generators other than the logical), and the \
logical ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],
 " pair we will use later:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"codes", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"<|", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<bit-flip\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"<|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<state\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<ZZI\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<IZZ\>\"", ",", 
            " ", "\"\<ZZZ\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<checks\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<ZZI\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<IZZ\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<logicals\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<XXX\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<ZII\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
       "|>"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<phase-flip\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"<|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<state\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           
           RowBox[{"\"\<XXI\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<IXX\>\"", ",", 
            " ", "\"\<XXX\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<checks\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<XXI\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<IXX\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<logicals\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<XII\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<ZZZ\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
       "|>"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<5-qubit\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"<|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<state\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", "\"\<5QubitCode\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
        "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<checks\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Most", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", "\"\<5QubitCode\>\"", "]"}], 
           "[", "\"\<Stabilizers\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<logicals\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<XXXXX\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<ZZZZZ\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], 
       "|>"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Steane\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"<|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<state\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", "\"\<SteaneCode\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
        "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<checks\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Most", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", "\"\<SteaneCode\>\"", "]"}], 
           "[", "\"\<Stabilizers\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<logicals\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<XXXXXXX\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<ZZZZZZZ\>\""}], "}"}]}]}],
        "|>"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Shor\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"<|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<state\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", "\"\<9QubitCode\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
        "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<checks\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Most", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", "\"\<9QubitCode\>\"", "]"}], 
           "[", "\"\<Stabilizers\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<logicals\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<XXXXXXXXX\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<ZZZZZZZZZ\>\""}], 
          "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}]}], "\n", "   ", "|>"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Keys", "[", "codes", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1435697913,ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"bit-flip\"\>", ",", "\<\"phase-flip\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"5-qubit\"\>", ",", "\<\"Steane\"\>", ",", "\<\"Shor\"\>"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[3]= ",
 CellID->1033213401,ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["A Sign-Exact +1 Codeword", "Subsection",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first thing to get right is the sign. \"The state is a codeword\" has \
to mean the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 " eigenstate of every generator, with the sign exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " and not ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 ", because a stabilizer with the wrong sign describes a different state \
entirely. We check this at the level of the state vector, comparing vectors \
rather than fidelities, so a sign error cannot hide. The shipped state has \
exact algebraic amplitudes (the Steane codeword's entries are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    SqrtBox["2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 ", for instance), so the comparison is a symbolic zero test, not a numerical \
tolerance."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build the Pauli operators as honest matrices (qubit 1 as the leftmost \
tensor factor, the ordering ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 " uses), read the state vector, and confirm each generator, sign included, \
leaves it fixed exactly:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"strip", "[", "s_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"StringDelete", "[", 
    RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"StartOfString", " ", "~~", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<+\>\"", " ", "|", " ", "\"\<-\>\""}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"sgn", "[", "s_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"If", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"StringStartsQ", "[", 
      RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", "\"\<-\>\""}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"pauliOp", "[", "s_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"sgn", "[", "s", "]"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"Fold", "[", 
     RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Characters", "[", 
          RowBox[{"strip", "[", "s", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "/.", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\"\<I\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<Y\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<Z\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "3"}]}], "}"}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
     "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"denseFixesQ", "[", "c_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<state\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<State\>\"", 
          "]"}], "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n",
      "   ", 
     RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<state\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Stabilizers\>\"", 
        "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"pauliOp", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "psi"}], " ", "-",
            " ", "psi"}], ",", " ", "PossibleZeroQ"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"denseFixesQ", " ", "/@", " ", "codes"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1772362660,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"bit-flip\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"phase-flip\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"5-qubit\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Steane\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Shor\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[4]= ",
 CellID->35498422,ExpressionUUID->"337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For every code, applying any generator to the codeword returns the codeword \
unchanged, exactly: the shipped state is a genuine ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 " codeword, sign included. The same exact amplitudes make normalization a \
symbolic identity, not a numerical near-miss, so each codeword has unit \
length as an exact statement:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
  RowBox[{"codes", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<state\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<State\>\"", 
           "]"}], "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "psi", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "psi"}], 
        "]"}], " ", "===", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->1407158826,ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[5]= ",
 CellID->1138490425,ExpressionUUID->"6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
This is the exactness a numeric fidelity would blur. Stim now enters as a \
second, independent engine, to confirm that these same generators form a \
consistent stabilizer group and read every syndrome the way the shipped \
engine does.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],

Cell["Opening a Stim Session", "Subsection",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The check so far lives entirely inside the Wolfram Language. A second, \
genuinely external opinion is worth having, and Stim is the natural source: \
the reference stabilizer simulator, written in C++, with an independent \
tableau engine. Open a Python session and confirm Stim is importable; if this \
reports Stim missing, install it with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"pip", " ", "install", " ", "stim"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 " into the Python that ",
 Cell[BoxData["ExternalEvaluate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 " uses, or skip the Stim cells and rely on the in-language checks."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"stimSession", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"StartExternalSession", "[", 
    RowBox[{"<|", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<System\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Python\>\""}], "|>"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"stimVersion", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Check", "[", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ExternalEvaluate", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "stimSession", ",", " ", "\"\<import stim; stim.__version__\>\""}], 
     "]"}], ",", "\n", 
    "   ", "\"\<stim not available: skip the Stim cells\>\""}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->2048061839,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell[BoxData["\<\"1.16.0\"\>"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[6]= ",
 CellID->1680809496,ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Stim reads identity as an underscore, so the only translation between the two \
sides is a character swap. Define that once and reuse it for the \
differentials below:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"toStim", "[", "s_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"StringReplace", "[", 
    RowBox[{"s", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<I\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<_\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell["Stim Accepts the Generators, and the Syndromes Agree", "Subsection",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two differentials carry Part A. The first hands Stim our stabilizer \
generators and asks whether they even form a consistent stabilizer group: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"stim", ".", "Tableau", ".", "from_stabilizers"}]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 " builds a tableau only if the generators are independent and mutually \
commuting, and it hands back its own canonical form of the same group. This \
is Stim vouching that the shipped generators describe a real stabilizer state."
}], "Text",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"stimGroupSize", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ExternalEvaluate", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "stimSession", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<\ndef group_size(gens):\n    t = \
stim.Tableau.from_stabilizers([stim.PauliString(g) for g in gens], \
allow_redundant=False, allow_underconstrained=False)\n    return \
len(t.to_stabilizers(canonicalize=True))\ngroup_size\>\""}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"stimAcceptsQ", "[", "c_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"gens", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"toStim", " ", "/@", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<state\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Stabilizers\>\"",
          "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"stimGroupSize", "[", "gens", "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Length", "[", "gens", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"stimAcceptsQ", " ", "/@", " ", "codes"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->768012750,ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"bit-flip\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"phase-flip\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"5-qubit\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Steane\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Shor\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[8]= ",
 CellID->1037501394,ExpressionUUID->"6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The second differential is the one that matters most for interoperability, \
because the syndrome is exactly what a real decoder consumes. For an error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["E", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " on a codeword, the syndrome bit of a check ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["g", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 " when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["E", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],
 " commutes with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["g", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 " when it anticommutes. On the Wolfram side we apply the error to the \
shipped state and read each check's expectation value; on the Stim side it is \
a commutation test. Compare them, for every code, across all weight-one and \
weight-two errors:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"weightK", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "k_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"If", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"k", " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"StringRepeat", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<I\>\"", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Catenate", "@", 
      RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
         RowBox[{"pos", ",", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"StringJoin", " ", "/@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ReplacePart", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"\"\<I\>\"", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"pos", " ", "->", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
              "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"{", 
                
                RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<Y\>\"", ",", 
                 " ", "\"\<Z\>\""}], "}"}], ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}]}], 
            ")"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"Subsets", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Range", "[", "n", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "k", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"applyErr", "[", 
    RowBox[{"ps_", ",", " ", "e_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Fold", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"With", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"StringTake", "[", 
           RowBox[{"e", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "#2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"If", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"c", " ", "===", " ", "\"\<I\>\""}], ",", " ", "#1", ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"#1", "[", 
           RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "#2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}],
      ",", "\n", "   ", "ps", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
      RowBox[{"StringLength", "[", "e", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ourSyndrome", "[", 
    RowBox[{"c_", ",", " ", "e_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"applyErr", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<state\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", "e"}], "]"}], 
          "[", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<Expectation\>\"", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
        " ", "/@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], ")"}], "/", 
    "2"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"stimSyndrome", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ExternalEvaluate", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "stimSession", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<\ndef stim_syndrome(gens, err):\n    e = stim.PauliString(err)\
\n    return [0 if stim.PauliString(g).commutes(e) else 1 for g in gens]\n\
stim_syndrome\>\""}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"syndromeMatchesStimQ", "[", "c_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"errs", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"weightK", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<state\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Qubits\>\"", 
            "]"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"weightK", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<state\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Qubits\>\"", 
            "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ourSyndrome", "[", 
          RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
        "errs"}], ")"}], " ", "===", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"stimSyndrome", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"toStim", " ", "/@", " ", 
            RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"toStim", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
        " ", "errs"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"syndromeMatchesStimQ", " ", "/@", " ", "codes"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->201914069,ExpressionUUID->"58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"bit-flip\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"phase-flip\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"5-qubit\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Steane\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Shor\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[9]= ",
 CellID->607076188,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
For every code, the shipped engine's syndrome and Stim's syndrome agree on \
the entire weight-one and weight-two error set, which is hundreds of errors \
for the larger codes. Combined with the sign-exact codeword above and Stim's \
acceptance of the generators, the shipped stabilizer layer and Stim describe \
the same states and read the same syndromes, wherever the two overlap.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell["The One Thing Stim Cannot Do: A Symbolic Measurement", "Subsection",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Everything so far Stim can also do, and does. Here is something it \
structurally cannot. A measurement outcome that is a genuine coin flip need \
not be drawn as a number; it can be carried as a ",
 StyleBox["symbol", "TI"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 "'s ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<SymbolicMeasure\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 " writes each unresolved random outcome as a fresh formal bit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],
 " inside a stabilizer sign, so the whole state stays a single object and the \
measurement is deferred, not sampled. Measure qubit 1 of a Bell pair \
symbolically and read the generators:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sm", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", "2", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<CNOT\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<SymbolicMeasure\>\"", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"sm", "[", "\"\<Stabilizers\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->1491197753,ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"1 - 2*\[FormalS][1]*ZI\"\>", ",", "\<\"ZZ\"\>"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[10]= ",
 CellID->518839321,ExpressionUUID->"58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The sign of the first generator now carries a formal bit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 " (displayed as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 " here; the subscript is a running session counter, so a re-run allocates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "3"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 ", and so on), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["s", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 ": the formal bit ",
 StyleBox["is", "TI"],
 " the unmade measurement. Extract whichever bit was allocated and substitute \
both values to reproduce the two post-measurement branches exactly:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Cases", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"sm", "[", "\"\<Phase\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[FormalS]", "[", "_", "]"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], 
     "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"sm", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<SubstituteOutcomes\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"s", " ", "->", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<Stabilizers\>\"", "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"sm", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<SubstituteOutcomes\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"s", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<Stabilizers\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1596700196,ExpressionUUID->"6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"ZI\"\>", ",", "\<\"ZZ\"\>"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\<\"-ZI\"\>", ",", "\<\"ZZ\"\>"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[11]= ",
 CellID->1663427655,ExpressionUUID->"4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The deeper point is that a formal bit is spent only where the randomness is \
genuine. Prepare two qubits in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"+"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 ", so each carries a fair-coin ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 "-outcome, and copy their parity onto a third with two ",
 Cell[BoxData["CNOT"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 "s. The prepared state carries a conserved ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 "-parity, the stabilizer ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "3"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"parityCode", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PauliStabilizer", "[", "3", "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<H\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<CNOT\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"parityCode", "[", "\"\<Stabilizers\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->521043313,ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"XIX\"\>", ",", "\<\"IXX\"\>", ",", "\<\"ZZZ\"\>"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[12]= ",
 CellID->1864044787,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The last generator, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "3"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],
 ", is the conservation law: because it stabilizes the state, the three ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 "-outcomes cannot be independent. Measuring all three symbolically therefore \
allocates only two formal bits, one per genuinely random qubit, not three:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"smPar", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"parityCode", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<SymbolicMeasure\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"freeBits", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"DeleteDuplicates", "@", 
   RowBox[{"Cases", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"smPar", "[", "\"\<Phase\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[FormalS]", "[", "_", "]"}], ",", " ", "Infinity"}], 
    "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->1062924604,ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[FormalS]", "[", "2", "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\[FormalS]", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[13]= ",
 CellID->827610706,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two bits, not three. Substituting them over all four assignments and \
reading each collapsed outcome exhibits the third bit as the sum of the first \
two, exactly what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "3"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 " demands:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"readBits", "[", "ps_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Keys", "@", 
     RowBox[{"Select", "[", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"AssociationThread", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ps", "[", "\"\<Qubits\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"ps", "[", "\"\<State\>\"", "]"}], 
           "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"#", " ", "=!=", " ", "0"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"readBits", "[", 
    RowBox[{"smPar", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<SubstituteOutcomes\>\"", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
       RowBox[{"freeBits", " ", "->", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
   "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Length", "[", "freeBits", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->57724831,ExpressionUUID->"6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[14]= ",
 CellID->554633244,ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The third bit is the sum of the first two in every row, consistent with the \
conserved ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "3"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],
 ": the engine spent a formal bit only on the genuine coins and left the \
determined outcome to follow. That parity is the syndrome of the simplest \
possible code, a single ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 "-check. The same idea drives fault-frame propagation, where a fault written \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["s", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],
 " a formal bit makes each syndrome an explicit function of the fault bits; \
propagating faults to syndromes for millions of shots is the acknowledged \
bottleneck of stabilizer simulation, and a symbolic sign turns \"re-traverse \
the circuit per shot\" into \"traverse once, then substitute.\" A discrete \
stabilizer sampler has no way to hold that symbol."
}], "Text",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],

Cell["\<\
Part III (Part B): An Independent Exact Analysis, Cross-Checked Against Stim\
\>", "Section",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell["\<\
The shipped engine reports syndromes and states. It does not, on its own, \
hand you the exact code distance or a lightest logical operator, and neither \
does Stim. Part B builds that exact analysis from the ground up, in a few \
small functions over GF(2), and then checks its answers both against the \
definition and against Stim. Rebuilding the linear algebra from scratch \
(rather than calling a packaged distance routine to check itself) is also the \
cleanest way to watch the machinery turn.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell["The Symplectic Picture: A Pauli as a Vector over GF(2)", "Subsection",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Each Pauli string on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 " qubits becomes a binary vector of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 ": an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],
 " contributes to the first half, a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],
 " to the second, a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Y", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 " to both. Two Paulis commute exactly when a bilinear form over GF(2), the \
symplectic product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 ", vanishes between their vectors. Define the per-letter rule, the vector, \
and the product:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xzOf", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"<|", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<I\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Y\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Z\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]}]}], "|>"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "s_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"p", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"xzOf", " ", "/@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Characters", "[", 
         RowBox[{"strip", "[", "s", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"p", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"p", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"omega", "[", 
    RowBox[{"u_", ",", " ", "v_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Length", "[", "u", "]"}], "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Take", "[", 
          RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Drop", "[", 
          RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Drop", "[", 
          RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Take", "[", 
          RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"omega", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "\"\<XII\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "\"\<ZII\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"omega", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "\"\<XII\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "\"\<IZI\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->2070168666,ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[15]= ",
 CellID->460230490,ExpressionUUID->"657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 " anticommute (they share a qubit and disagree there), while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 " commute (they act on different qubits). This single function is the whole \
notion of \"detectable\": the syndrome of an error is just its symplectic \
product against each generator."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell["Distance from First Principles", "Subsection",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A Pauli is a logical operator when it lies in the normalizer but not in the \
stabilizer group: it commutes with every generator (zero syndrome) ",
 StyleBox["and", "TI"],
 " it is not itself a product of generators. The second condition is the one \
that is easy to get backwards. Membership in the group is a GF(2) span \
question, and the correct test is that appending the candidate's vector to \
the check matrix leaves the rank unchanged; so \"not in the group\" means the \
rank strictly ",
 StyleBox["rises", "TI"],
 ". Spell that out as ",
 Cell[BoxData["logicalVecQ"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],
 ", then make the distance a weight-increasing search that stops at the first \
logical it finds. The search builds the check matrix and its rank once and \
reuses them across every candidate, rather than rebuilding them at each \
step:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"rank2", "[", "rows_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"MatrixRank", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rows", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Modulus", " ", "->", " ", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"logicalVecQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{"checks_", ",", " ", "v_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"sg", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"symOf", " ", "/@", " ", "checks"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"rank2", "[", "sg", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
         RowBox[{"sg", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"omega", "[", 
             RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ", "0"}], " ",
            "&"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"rank2", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
           RowBox[{"sg", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ">", " ", 
         "m"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"distanceWitness", "[", "checks_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"sg", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"symOf", " ", "/@", " ", "checks"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"StringLength", "[", 
         RowBox[{"strip", "[", 
          RowBox[{"First", "[", "checks", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"rank2", "[", "sg", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"With", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"logicalQ", " ", "=", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
            RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
               RowBox[{"sg", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"omega", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"v", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
                  "0"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"rank2", "[", 
                RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"sg", ",", " ", "v"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ">", " ", 
               "m"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"Catch", "[", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Scan", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
              RowBox[{"w", ",", "\n", "        ", 
               RowBox[{"With", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"{", 
                  RowBox[{"cand", " ", "=", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"SelectFirst", "[", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"weightK", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "w"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"logicalQ", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}]}], 
                    "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "         ", 
                 RowBox[{"If", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"!", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"MissingQ", "[", "cand", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
                   RowBox[{"Throw", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"{", 
                    RowBox[{"w", ",", " ", "cand"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
                "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "       ", 
             RowBox[{"Range", "[", "n", "]"}]}], "]"}], ";", "\n", "      ", 
           RowBox[{"Missing", "[", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"distanceWitness", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"codes", "[", "\"\<5-qubit\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", 
   "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->750476119,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"3", ",", "\<\"XYXII\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[16]= ",
 CellID->1121406919,ExpressionUUID->"6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The output is a weight and a witness at that weight: a lightest logical for \
the five-qubit code, found by our own search with no reference to any \
distance routine. Its weight is the code distance. Now put the whole table \
together, showing each code's parameters, the independent distance, and the \
witness the search returned:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Grid", "[", "\n", "   ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Prepend", "[", "\n", "    ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
       RowBox[{"name", ",", "\n", "     ", 
        RowBox[{"With", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
             RowBox[{"codes", "[", "name", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"n", " ", "=", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"codes", "[", "name", "]"}], "[", "\"\<state\>\"", 
               "]"}], "[", "\"\<Qubits\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"dw", " ", "=", " ", 
             RowBox[{"distanceWitness", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"codes", "[", "name", "]"}], "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", 
               "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"name", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"StringJoin", "[", 
             RowBox[{"\"\<[[\>\"", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"ToString", "[", "n", "]"}], ",", " ", "\"\<,\>\"", ",",
               " ", 
              RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
               RowBox[{"n", " ", "-", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",",
               " ", "\"\<,\>\"", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
               RowBox[{"dw", "[", 
                RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
              " ", "\"\<]]\>\""}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"dw", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "/@",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"Keys", "[", "codes", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Style", "[", 
        RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "Bold"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<code\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<[[n,k,d]]\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<witness\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Alignment", " ", "->", " ", "Left"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Spacings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "0.8"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1725217879,ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"code\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"[[n,k,d]]\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"witness\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"bit-flip\"\>", "\<\"[[3,1,1]]\"\>", "\<\"ZII\"\>"},
    {"\<\"phase-flip\"\>", "\<\"[[3,1,1]]\"\>", "\<\"XII\"\>"},
    {"\<\"5-qubit\"\>", "\<\"[[5,1,3]]\"\>", "\<\"XYXII\"\>"},
    {"\<\"Steane\"\>", "\<\"[[7,1,3]]\"\>", "\<\"XXXIIII\"\>"},
    {"\<\"Shor\"\>", "\<\"[[9,1,3]]\"\>", "\<\"XXXIIIIII\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{2}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[17]= ",
 CellID->1590527600,ExpressionUUID->"7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The Shor, five-qubit, and Steane codes come out as the familiar \
distance-three codes. The two three-qubit codes come out at distance one, \
which is the honest surprise of the whole subject.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],

Cell["\<\
The Honest Surprise: A Repetition Code Has Quantum Distance One\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The three-qubit bit-flip code is often introduced as a distance-three code, \
and as a ",
 StyleBox["classical", "TI"],
 " code against bit flips it is. As a ",
 StyleBox["quantum", "TI"],
 " code it is not. Look at the syndrome of a single ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],
 " on the first qubit, and ask whether that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],
 " is a logical operator:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"codes", "[", "\"\<bit-flip\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"omega", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "\"\<ZII\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ", "0"}], 
      " ", "&"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"logicalVecQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"codes", "[", "\"\<bit-flip\>\"", "]"}], "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "\"\<ZII\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->1476261556,ExpressionUUID->"2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[18]= ",
 CellID->1373722967,ExpressionUUID->"362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The lone ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],
 " commutes with both ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],
 "-type checks, so it is undetectable, yet it is not in the stabilizer group, \
so it acts nontrivially on the codespace. It is therefore a weight-one \
logical, and the quantum code distance is one. In words, protecting against \
bit flips with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 "-type checks leaves phase errors completely unguarded, and a single \
unguarded phase error is a logical fault. This is not a defect in the \
computation; it is the reason a real code protects against both error types, \
which is exactly what the Shor code does by nesting the two repetition ideas. \
The analysis reports the mathematics, not the folklore."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],

Cell["Logical Operators and Their Algebra", "Subsection",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A code with one logical qubit comes with a logical pair ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],
 " that must obey the algebra of a bare qubit: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 " anticommutes with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 ", both commute with every stabilizer, and neither lies in the group. Check \
the whole algebra independently with the symplectic product and the rank \
test, for every code:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"logicalAlgebraQ", "[", "c_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"sg", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"symOf", " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"xbar", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<logicals\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"zbar", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<logicals\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"rank2", "[", "sg", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"And", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"omega", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "xbar", "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "zbar", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
          "1"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"omega", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "xbar", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
             "0"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"omega", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "zbar", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
             "0"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"rank2", "[", 
           RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
            RowBox[{"sg", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "xbar", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ">", 
          " ", "m"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"rank2", "[", 
           RowBox[{"Append", "[", 
            RowBox[{"sg", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "zbar", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ">", 
          " ", "m"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"logicalAlgebraQ", " ", "/@", " ", "codes"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->620178773,ExpressionUUID->"6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"bit-flip\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"phase-flip\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"5-qubit\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Steane\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Shor\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[19]= ",
 CellID->1392267381,ExpressionUUID->"612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every code's logical pair passes the full algebra check. Note that the \
minimum-weight witness from the distance search need not be one of these \
canonical operators: the logical pair is a valid ",
 StyleBox["generating", "TI"],
 " set, while the witness is the lightest element of the whole coset, and the \
two answer different questions."
}], "Text",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell["Stim Confirms the Witness", "Subsection",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Stim can certify the distance witness without enumerating a single error. A \
minimum-weight logical must be ",
 StyleBox["undetectable", "TI"],
 " (it commutes with every check) and ",
 StyleBox["nontrivial", "TI"],
 " (it anticommutes with at least one logical operator, so it acts on the \
codespace). Those two facts together place it in the normalizer but outside \
the stabilizer group, which is the definition of a logical. Ask Stim for both:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"stimWitness", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ExternalEvaluate", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "stimSession", ",", 
     " ", "\"\<\ndef stim_witness(gens, logs, w):\n    W = \
stim.PauliString(w)\n    undetectable = all(stim.PauliString(g).commutes(W) \
for g in gens)\n    nontrivial = any(not stim.PauliString(p).commutes(W) for \
p in logs)\n    return [bool(undetectable), bool(nontrivial)]\nstim_witness\>\
\""}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"stimWitnessQ", "[", "c_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"w", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"distanceWitness", "[", 
         RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"stimWitness", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"toStim", " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<checks\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"toStim", " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<logicals\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"toStim", "[", "w", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"True", ",", " ", "True"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"stimWitnessQ", " ", "/@", " ", "codes"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->1100849853,ExpressionUUID->"25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\<\"bit-flip\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"phase-flip\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"5-qubit\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Steane\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"\<\"Shor\"\>", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], 
  "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[20]= ",
 CellID->1468330830,ExpressionUUID->"574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For each code Stim reports the witness as both undetectable and nontrivial. \
Stim vouches that the witness is a genuine logical; the ",
 StyleBox["minimality", "TI"],
 " of its weight, that nothing lighter is logical, is what our exhaustive \
symplectic search established, and it is the part no sampler provides. The \
division of labor is the honest one: Stim confirms the witness is real, and \
the exact search confirms it is the lightest."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell["Part IV: A Parameter Stim Cannot Carry", "Section",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],

Cell["\<\
Everything so far was a concrete code at a concrete size. The \
exact-and-symbolic corner has one more move, the one with no numeric \
counterpart: hold a parameter symbolic and certify a whole family, or a whole \
continuum, at once.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],

Cell["A Family Indexed by n", "Subsection",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Take the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "2"}], ",", "2"}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 " code family: two generators, an all-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],
 " string and an all-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],
 " string, on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],
 " qubits. Their symplectic product is a sum of per-qubit overlaps, and the \
all-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],
 " and all-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],
 " strings meet on every qubit, so each of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],
 " qubits contributes a ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],
 " and the product is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"omegaXZ", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Sum", "[", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "n"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->879243051,ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],

Cell[BoxData["n"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[21]= ",
 CellID->1610719777,ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Carried symbolically, the product is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],
 ". The generators commute when it is even and anticommute when it is odd. \
Substitute an even index ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 " and an odd index ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "2", 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],
 " and reduce the commutator mod 2 to derive both cases at once, in the \
integer ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"omegaXZ", " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"n", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}]}]}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Mod", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"omegaXZ", " ", "/.", " ", 
        RowBox[{"n", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "k"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}]}], ",", " ", "2"}], 
      "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"k", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Integers"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->1818488019,ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[22]= ",
 CellID->1752175041,ExpressionUUID->"3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two parities are ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 ": the family is a genuine code exactly on the even integers, and an odd ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],
 " has no code at all. That is derived for the whole family in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],
 ", not checked case by case."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2099309037,ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The distance is a size-independent argument the from-scratch search then \
confirms at sample sizes. Build the family's checks at any size, and put a \
candidate weight-two operator, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],
 ", to the same logical test the concrete codes used:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->512383039,ExpressionUUID->"66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"familyChecks", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"StringRepeat", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<X\>\"", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"StringRepeat", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Z\>\"", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"logicalVecQ", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"familyChecks", "[", "6", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"symOf", "[", "\"\<XXIIII\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->688684714,ExpressionUUID->"0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[23]= ",
 CellID->1478107962,ExpressionUUID->"0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],
 " is a logical: it meets the all-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],
 " generator on two qubits (an even overlap, so it commutes), meets the \
all-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],
 " generator trivially, and is not a product of the generators. That argument \
is size-independent, even though the check above ran at a representative ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["X", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 " has weight two for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[GreaterEqual]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 ", while the only nontrivial group elements are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"\[CircleTimes]", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"\[CircleTimes]", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"\[CircleTimes]", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],
 ", each of weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 ", so the lightest logical has weight two whenever ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "<", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 " and no weight-one error slips through. Run the search at several sizes to \
confirm the distance lands where the argument says:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1809098798,ExpressionUUID->"6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"distanceWitness", "[", 
     RowBox[{"familyChecks", "[", "n", "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "6", ",", " ", "8", ",", " ", "10"}], "}"}]}], 
    "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->308320186,ExpressionUUID->"54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"2", ",", "2", ",", "2", ",", "2"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[24]= ",
 CellID->845252322,ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A numeric simulator has to instantiate a specific ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],
 " to say anything at all; it can confirm any number of cases but never the \
family. The repetition family ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],
 " yields to the same treatment. Its checks are the neighboring ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],
 "-pairs, which generate the even-weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],
 "-strings, so a lone ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],
 " commutes with all of them yet is not their product: an undetectable \
weight-one logical, for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->724760089,ExpressionUUID->"33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"repChecks", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"StringJoin", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"ReplacePart", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
          RowBox[{"\"\<I\>\"", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Z\>\""}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"#", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], " ", "->", 
            " ", "\"\<Z\>\""}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
       RowBox[{"n", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"distanceWitness", "[", 
  RowBox[{"repChecks", "[", "7", "]"}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->310708056,ExpressionUUID->"794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "\<\"ZIIIIII\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[25]= ",
 CellID->653431539,ExpressionUUID->"167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A single undetectable ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],
 ", of weight one: the repetition code's quantum distance is one for the \
whole family, the honest surprise of Part B stated once for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->811283638,ExpressionUUID->"285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],

Cell["A Continuous Error Angle", "Subsection",
 CellID->207978548,ExpressionUUID->"57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Symbolic generality reaches continuous parameters too, which is where a \
Pauli-sampling simulator has nothing to say. Consider a ",
 StyleBox["coherent", "TI"],
 " error on the bit-flip codeword: not a discrete bit flip, but a rotation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["X", "TI"], "/", "2"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],
 " on the first qubit, through a symbolic angle. The state stays a \
superposition of \"no error\" and \"flipped,\" and the syndrome operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],
 " has an expectation value that is an exact function of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->437474228,ExpressionUUID->"457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"psi0", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", "->", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "8"}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"vTheta", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<RX\>\"", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", "1"}], 
        "}"}], "]"}], "[", "psi0", "]"}], "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"zzOp", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"zzExpectation", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "vTheta", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "zzOp", " ", ".",
      " ", "vTheta"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->590983534,ExpressionUUID->"499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[26]= ",
 CellID->1257758076,ExpressionUUID->"0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The rotation is unitary, so the state it produces stays normalized at every \
angle, and the expectation above is read in a properly normalized state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->11631581,ExpressionUUID->"0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "vTheta", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "vTheta"}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->300639476,ExpressionUUID->"6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],

Cell[BoxData["1"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[27]= ",
 CellID->902677572,ExpressionUUID->"2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The syndrome expectation itself is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],
 ": it interpolates continuously from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],
 " (no error, the codeword is untouched) to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],
 " (a full bit flip, a definite nonzero syndrome), passing through zero at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],
 " (a maximally uncertain syndrome). A coherent rotation is non-Clifford, so \
it lives in the exact dense simulator, not in a stabilizer tableau; carrying \
the angle symbolically returns the whole error curve as a closed form. This \
is the natural language for coherent-error and threshold questions, and it is \
exactly the representation a discrete stabilizer sampler cannot produce."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1055776787,ExpressionUUID->"11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"zzExpectation", " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"zzExpectation", " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"zzExpectation", " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "->", " ", "Pi"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->1532176256,ExpressionUUID->"473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "0", ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[28]= ",
 CellID->660101777,ExpressionUUID->"12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The three sampled values confirm the endpoints and the midpoint of the closed \
form we just derived.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1348896709,ExpressionUUID->"1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The endpoints are the whole story only at large angle. For a ",
 StyleBox["weak", "TI"],
 " coherent error the quantity that matters is the probability that the \
syndrome fires, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "-", 
    StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "1"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["Z", "TI"], "2"]}], 
    StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],
 ", and its behavior as the rotation turns on is the leading term of its \
series in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1427211115,ExpressionUUID->"5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Normal", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Series", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "zzExpectation"}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->4772748,ExpressionUUID->"5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FractionBox[
  SuperscriptBox["\[Theta]", "2"], "4"]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[29]= ",
 CellID->720647268,ExpressionUUID->"621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To leading order the syndrome fires with probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],
 ": the coherent-error rate is quadratic in the rotation angle, vanishing \
faster than linearly as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],
 ". That small-angle rate is a continuous-parameter statement a discrete \
bit-flip channel cannot make, and it is the kind of input a threshold \
calculation actually consumes."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1402006442,ExpressionUUID->"4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],

Cell["Part V: Where This Leaves Us", "Section",
 CellID->1901179466,ExpressionUUID->"494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],

Cell["\<\
Before we close, a plain summary of what has been established:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->210724908,ExpressionUUID->"39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],

Cell["\<\
For every one of the five codes, applying any shipped generator to the \
codeword leaves it fixed exactly, sign included; Stim accepts the same \
generators as a consistent stabilizer group; and the shipped syndrome equals \
Stim's across every weight-one and weight-two error.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1992790374,ExpressionUUID->"4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],
 "'s symbolic measurement carries a random outcome as a formal bit, and a \
forced outcome comes back as an explicit function of the free bits, which a \
discrete sampler cannot represent."
}], "Item",
 CellID->292747604,ExpressionUUID->"4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],

Cell["\<\
An independent GF(2) search returns the exact distance and a minimum-weight \
witness for each code; the logical operators satisfy the full commutation \
algebra; and Stim confirms each witness is a genuine logical, while the \
exhaustive search establishes it is the lightest.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1553818268,ExpressionUUID->"16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "2"}], ",", "2"}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],
 " code condition is derived at symbolic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],
 ", its distance argued size-independently and confirmed at sample sizes; the \
repetition family's distance is one; and a coherent error's syndrome is \
returned as the exact function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],
 ", with a small-angle syndrome rate of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1870754514,ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],

Cell["\<\
The picture is a clean division of labor. Stim owns scale and speed: sampling \
large circuits, benchmarking decoders, estimating thresholds. The shipped \
stabilizer layer, checked here against Stim, gets the states, signs, and \
syndromes exactly right and drops into the rest of a quantum-mechanics \
toolkit; and the Wolfram Language around it owns the small-and-certain \
corner, the exact minimum distance, a witness for it, the logical algebra, \
and, uniquely, the ability to hold a parameter symbolic and certify an entire \
family or a continuous error at once. The two agree wherever they overlap, \
which is what makes the exact answers trustworthy and the symbolic ones worth \
reaching for.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1358728755,ExpressionUUID->"60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The honest boundary is worth restating: exact minimum distance is NP-hard, \
so the distance search is a small-code instrument by mathematical necessity, \
not a scaling competitor. When you want the exact answer for a textbook code, \
or a statement about a whole family, the exactness and the symbol are the \
point; when you want a threshold for a distance-25 surface code, reach for \
Stim. Both live in the same notebook, and now you can check one against the \
other yourself. To push further: feed your own stabilizer generators into ",
 Cell[BoxData["PauliStabilizer"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],
 ", run the same independent checks, and diff against Stim; or take the \
symbolic-family argument to a code family of your own and see whether one \
evaluation can settle it."
}], "Text",
 CellID->935019337,ExpressionUUID->"23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"]
},
